            <div xml:id="d893">

                <pb facs="0970" n="960" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg960"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/12–2148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-12-24T14:00:00-05:00">December 24, 1948—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2259. Appreciate urtel 2851 Dec. 21. Dept anxiously awaiting replies from other
                    concerned departments to Dept’s previous requests that temporary haven in areas
                    under US control be granted refugees having end destination elsewhere.</p>
                <p>Will advise further when such replies received.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
